      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:201:5",
      "text": [
        " الصَّلَاةُ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ تَعْدِلُ مِائَةَ أَلْفِ صَلَاةٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Abu Salma, from Haroun Bin Kharjat, from Samit, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, from his<sup>asws</sup> forefathers<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span> in the Sacred Masjid equates to one hundred thousand <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span>s (elsewhere)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ahmad ibn Muhammad has narrated from Ali ibn abu Salmah from Flarun ibn Kharijah from Samet who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has narrated from his ancestors, ‘Alayhim al-Salam, who have said that performing Salat (prayer) in Masjid al-Haram is equal to one hundred thousand Salat (prayer) elsewhere.” "
        ]
      }
